[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":2032},["ShallowReactive",2],{"page-\u002Frust\u002F20-modules-and-crates":3},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":16,"extension":2026,"meta":2027,"navigation":953,"path":2028,"seo":2029,"stem":2030,"__hash__":2031},"content\u002Frust\u002F20-modules-and-crates.md","20 — Modules, Crates, Packages & Paths",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":1982},"minimark",[9,13,17,22,67,71,76,96,175,189,193,203,212,219,223,238,275,288,426,430,477,480,487,531,534,546,563,605,609,712,715,768,771,775,779,808,814,818,847,851,855,880,886,895,903,907,982,989,993,1021,1046,1056,1060,1064,1087,1127,1138,1142,1146,1184,1192,1220,1226,1230,1234,1242,1246,1278,1282,1410,1417,1425,1429,1514,1518,1604,1608,1615,1793,1920,1924,1953,1956,1975,1978],[10,11,5],"h1",{"id":12},"_20-modules-crates-packages-paths",[14,15,16],"p",{},"Rust's module system controls visibility, organization, and namespacing.",[18,19,21],"h2",{"id":20},"definitions","Definitions",[23,24,25,38,52,58],"ul",{},[26,27,28,32,33,37],"li",{},[29,30,31],"strong",{},"Package",": a Cargo project (a ",[34,35,36],"code",{},"Cargo.toml"," + one or more crates).",[26,39,40,43,44,47,48,51],{},[29,41,42],{},"Crate",": a compilation unit (binary or library). Root file (",[34,45,46],{},"main.rs","\u002F",[34,49,50],{},"lib.rs",").",[26,53,54,57],{},[29,55,56],{},"Module",": a named scope inside a crate. Controls visibility.",[26,59,60,63,64,51],{},[29,61,62],{},"Path",": how you reference an item (",[34,65,66],{},"crate::foo::bar",[18,68,70],{"id":69},"module-declaration","Module Declaration",[72,73,75],"h3",{"id":74},"why-the-module-system-exists","Why the module system exists",[14,77,78,79,82,83,87,88,91,92,95],{},"Rust's module system ",[29,80,81],{},"separates code organization from file layout",": a module is a named ",[84,85,86],"em",{},"scope"," that controls visibility, and the file system is one (of several) ways to ",[84,89,90],{},"provide"," the module's contents. This decoupling means the same logical structure (",[34,93,94],{},"crate::network::server",") can live in one file or several, and you reorganize without rewriting paths. You split code into modules when a single file gets too large, when you want to enforce visibility boundaries (a public API surface backed by private internals), or when logical groupings (network, ui, db) make the codebase navigable. Reach for modules when \"one file\" stops scaling; keep one file when the code is small enough to grasp at once.",[97,98,100],"code-wrapper",{"language":99},"rust",[101,102,106],"pre",{"className":103,"code":104,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"language-rust shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","\u002F\u002F src\u002Flib.rs\nmod network;\nmod ui {\n    pub mod window;\n    pub mod button;\n}\n","",[34,107,108,117,132,143,157,169],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,110,113],"span",{"class":111,"line":112},"line",1,[109,114,116],{"class":115},"sdCPZ","\u002F\u002F src\u002Flib.rs\n",[109,118,120,124,128],{"class":111,"line":119},2,[109,121,123],{"class":122},"svdQ7","mod",[109,125,127],{"class":126},"sIsaT"," network",[109,129,131],{"class":130},"ssxIu",";\n",[109,133,135,137,140],{"class":111,"line":134},3,[109,136,123],{"class":122},[109,138,139],{"class":126}," ui",[109,141,142],{"class":130}," {\n",[109,144,146,149,152,155],{"class":111,"line":145},4,[109,147,148],{"class":122},"    pub",[109,150,151],{"class":122}," mod",[109,153,154],{"class":126}," window",[109,156,131],{"class":130},[109,158,160,162,164,167],{"class":111,"line":159},5,[109,161,148],{"class":122},[109,163,151],{"class":122},[109,165,166],{"class":126}," button",[109,168,131],{"class":130},[109,170,172],{"class":111,"line":171},6,[109,173,174],{"class":130},"}\n",[14,176,177,180,181,184,185,188],{},[34,178,179],{},"mod network;"," looks for ",[34,182,183],{},"network.rs"," or ",[34,186,187],{},"network\u002Fmod.rs"," (legacy) and includes it as a submodule.",[18,190,192],{"id":191},"file-layout-conventions-2018","File Layout Conventions (2018+)",[97,194,196],{"language":195},"text",[101,197,201],{"className":198,"code":200,"language":195,"meta":105},[199],"language-text","src\u002F\n├── lib.rs            \u002F\u002F crate root: `pub mod ...`\n├── main.rs\n├── network.rs        \u002F\u002F corresponds to `mod network;`\n└── network\u002F\n    └── server.rs     \u002F\u002F corresponds to `mod server;` *inside* network.rs\n",[34,202,200],{"__ignoreMap":105},[14,204,205,206,208,209,211],{},"The 2018 edition prefers ",[34,207,183],{}," over ",[34,210,187],{},". Don't mix the two for the same module.",[18,213,215,218],{"id":214},"use-importing",[34,216,217],{},"use"," — Importing",[72,220,222],{"id":221},"when-to-use-each-path-form","When to use each path form",[14,224,225,226,229,230,233,234,237],{},"Rust deliberately doesn't ",[29,227,228],{},"auto-import"," anything (no global prelude beyond ",[34,231,232],{},"std::prelude",") — every import is explicit so you always know where a name comes from. The path forms differ by ",[84,235,236],{},"what they're relative to",":",[23,239,240,252,267],{},[26,241,242,247,248,251],{},[29,243,244],{},[34,245,246],{},"crate::"," — absolute from the crate root. Use when you want a stable path that doesn't change if you move the ",[84,249,250],{},"current"," file (the path is anchored to the crate, not the file's location).",[26,253,254,259,260,263,264,266],{},[29,255,256],{},[34,257,258],{},"super::"," — one module up (the parent). Use for siblings in the same parent module, but be aware it's ",[84,261,262],{},"relative",": moving the file changes what ",[34,265,258],{}," resolves to.",[26,268,269,274],{},[29,270,271],{},[34,272,273],{},"self::"," — the current module. Rare; mostly for disambiguation or for items defined in the same file you're importing into a nested scope.",[14,276,277,278,280,281,283,284,287],{},"Reach for ",[34,279,246],{}," in larger projects (it's stable under file moves); ",[34,282,258],{}," is fine for tightly-coupled sibling modules that move together. Aliasing (",[34,285,286],{},"as",") is for resolving name conflicts or shortening verbose paths.",[97,289,290],{"language":99},[101,291,293],{"className":103,"code":292,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"use std::collections::HashMap;\nuse std::io::{self, Read, Write};   \u002F\u002F bring multiple items\nuse std::io::Read as IoRead;        \u002F\u002F alias\nuse crate::network::server;          \u002F\u002F absolute path from crate root\nuse super::sibling;                  \u002F\u002F one module up\nuse self::inner;                     \u002F\u002F current module\n",[34,294,295,315,352,378,396,411],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,296,297,299,302,305,308,310,313],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,298,217],{"class":122},[109,300,301],{"class":126}," std",[109,303,304],{"class":122},"::",[109,306,307],{"class":126},"collections",[109,309,304],{"class":122},[109,311,312],{"class":126},"HashMap",[109,314,131],{"class":130},[109,316,317,319,321,323,326,328,331,335,338,341,343,346,349],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,318,217],{"class":122},[109,320,301],{"class":126},[109,322,304],{"class":122},[109,324,325],{"class":126},"io",[109,327,304],{"class":122},[109,329,330],{"class":130},"{",[109,332,334],{"class":333},"snvgF","self",[109,336,337],{"class":130},", ",[109,339,340],{"class":126},"Read",[109,342,337],{"class":130},[109,344,345],{"class":126},"Write",[109,347,348],{"class":130},"};   ",[109,350,351],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F bring multiple items\n",[109,353,354,356,358,360,362,364,366,369,372,375],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,355,217],{"class":122},[109,357,301],{"class":126},[109,359,304],{"class":122},[109,361,325],{"class":126},[109,363,304],{"class":122},[109,365,340],{"class":126},[109,367,368],{"class":122}," as",[109,370,371],{"class":126}," IoRead",[109,373,374],{"class":130},";        ",[109,376,377],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F alias\n",[109,379,380,382,385,388,390,393],{"class":111,"line":145},[109,381,217],{"class":122},[109,383,384],{"class":122}," crate::",[109,386,387],{"class":126},"network",[109,389,304],{"class":122},[109,391,392],{"class":130},"server;          ",[109,394,395],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F absolute path from crate root\n",[109,397,398,400,403,405,408],{"class":111,"line":159},[109,399,217],{"class":122},[109,401,402],{"class":333}," super",[109,404,304],{"class":122},[109,406,407],{"class":130},"sibling;                  ",[109,409,410],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F one module up\n",[109,412,413,415,418,420,423],{"class":111,"line":171},[109,414,217],{"class":122},[109,416,417],{"class":333}," self",[109,419,304],{"class":122},[109,421,422],{"class":130},"inner;                     ",[109,424,425],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F current module\n",[72,427,429],{"id":428},"glob-imports","Glob Imports",[97,431,432],{"language":99},[101,433,435],{"className":103,"code":434,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"use std::io::prelude::*;            \u002F\u002F rare; usually too broad\nuse crate::network::*;               \u002F\u002F bring all public items\n",[34,436,437,461],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,438,439,441,443,445,447,449,452,455,458],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,440,217],{"class":122},[109,442,301],{"class":126},[109,444,304],{"class":122},[109,446,325],{"class":126},[109,448,304],{"class":122},[109,450,451],{"class":126},"prelude",[109,453,454],{"class":122},"::*",[109,456,457],{"class":130},";            ",[109,459,460],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F rare; usually too broad\n",[109,462,463,465,467,469,471,474],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,464,217],{"class":122},[109,466,384],{"class":122},[109,468,387],{"class":126},[109,470,454],{"class":122},[109,472,473],{"class":130},";               ",[109,475,476],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F bring all public items\n",[14,478,479],{},"Avoid glob imports except for preludes.",[18,481,483,486],{"id":482},"pub-use-re-exports",[34,484,485],{},"pub use"," — Re-exports",[97,488,489],{"language":99},[101,490,492],{"className":103,"code":491,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"\u002F\u002F lib.rs\npub mod api;\npub use api::Client;   \u002F\u002F re-export so users can `use my_crate::Client`\n",[34,493,494,499,511],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,495,496],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,497,498],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F lib.rs\n",[109,500,501,504,506,509],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,502,503],{"class":122},"pub",[109,505,151],{"class":122},[109,507,508],{"class":126}," api",[109,510,131],{"class":130},[109,512,513,515,518,520,522,525,528],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,514,503],{"class":122},[109,516,517],{"class":122}," use",[109,519,508],{"class":126},[109,521,304],{"class":122},[109,523,524],{"class":126},"Client",[109,526,527],{"class":130},";   ",[109,529,530],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F re-export so users can `use my_crate::Client`\n",[14,532,533],{},"Re-export is the standard way to flatten the public API and hide internal structure.",[18,535,537,538,337,541,337,543],{"id":536},"paths-and-crate-self-super","Paths and ",[34,539,540],{},"crate",[34,542,334],{},[34,544,545],{},"super",[23,547,548,553,558],{},[26,549,550,552],{},[34,551,246],{}," — absolute from crate root.",[26,554,555,557],{},[34,556,273],{}," — current module.",[26,559,560,562],{},[34,561,258],{}," — parent module.",[97,564,565],{"language":99},[101,566,568],{"className":103,"code":567,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"\u002F\u002F in src\u002Fnetwork\u002Fserver.rs\nuse super::connection;     \u002F\u002F src\u002Fnetwork\u002Fconnection.rs\nuse crate::network::connection;   \u002F\u002F same, explicit\n",[34,569,570,575,589],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,571,572],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,573,574],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F in src\u002Fnetwork\u002Fserver.rs\n",[109,576,577,579,581,583,586],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,578,217],{"class":122},[109,580,402],{"class":333},[109,582,304],{"class":122},[109,584,585],{"class":130},"connection;     ",[109,587,588],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F src\u002Fnetwork\u002Fconnection.rs\n",[109,590,591,593,595,597,599,602],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,592,217],{"class":122},[109,594,384],{"class":122},[109,596,387],{"class":126},[109,598,304],{"class":122},[109,600,601],{"class":130},"connection;   ",[109,603,604],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F same, explicit\n",[18,606,608],{"id":607},"visibility","Visibility",[97,610,611],{"language":99},[101,612,614],{"className":103,"code":613,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"pub fn public_fn() {}            \u002F\u002F visible everywhere\nfn private_fn() {}                \u002F\u002F visible only in this module\npub(crate) fn internal() {}       \u002F\u002F visible within this crate only\npub(super) fn for_parent() {}     \u002F\u002F visible in parent module\npub(in path) fn scoped() {}       \u002F\u002F visible in a specific module path\n",[34,615,616,632,646,669,690],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,617,618,620,623,626,629],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,619,503],{"class":122},[109,621,622],{"class":122}," fn",[109,624,625],{"class":126}," public_fn",[109,627,628],{"class":130},"() {}            ",[109,630,631],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F visible everywhere\n",[109,633,634,637,640,643],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,635,636],{"class":122},"fn",[109,638,639],{"class":126}," private_fn",[109,641,642],{"class":130},"() {}                ",[109,644,645],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F visible only in this module\n",[109,647,648,650,653,655,658,660,663,666],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,649,503],{"class":122},[109,651,652],{"class":130},"(",[109,654,540],{"class":122},[109,656,657],{"class":130},") ",[109,659,636],{"class":122},[109,661,662],{"class":126}," internal",[109,664,665],{"class":130},"() {}       ",[109,667,668],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F visible within this crate only\n",[109,670,671,673,675,677,679,681,684,687],{"class":111,"line":145},[109,672,503],{"class":122},[109,674,652],{"class":130},[109,676,545],{"class":333},[109,678,657],{"class":130},[109,680,636],{"class":122},[109,682,683],{"class":126}," for_parent",[109,685,686],{"class":130},"() {}     ",[109,688,689],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F visible in parent module\n",[109,691,692,694,696,699,702,704,707,709],{"class":111,"line":159},[109,693,503],{"class":122},[109,695,652],{"class":130},[109,697,698],{"class":122},"in",[109,700,701],{"class":130}," path) ",[109,703,636],{"class":122},[109,705,706],{"class":126}," scoped",[109,708,665],{"class":130},[109,710,711],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F visible in a specific module path\n",[14,713,714],{},"Fields and variants have their own visibility:",[97,716,717],{"language":99},[101,718,720],{"className":103,"code":719,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"pub struct User {\n    pub name: String,\n    email: String,       \u002F\u002F private — only this module can construct\u002Fmodify\n}\n",[34,721,722,734,749,764],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,723,724,726,729,732],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,725,503],{"class":122},[109,727,728],{"class":122}," struct",[109,730,731],{"class":126}," User",[109,733,142],{"class":130},[109,735,736,738,741,743,746],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,737,148],{"class":122},[109,739,740],{"class":130}," name",[109,742,237],{"class":122},[109,744,745],{"class":126}," String",[109,747,748],{"class":130},",\n",[109,750,751,754,756,758,761],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,752,753],{"class":130},"    email",[109,755,237],{"class":122},[109,757,745],{"class":126},[109,759,760],{"class":130},",       ",[109,762,763],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F private — only this module can construct\u002Fmodify\n",[109,765,766],{"class":111,"line":145},[109,767,174],{"class":130},[14,769,770],{},"Enums' variants inherit the enum's visibility by default; you can override per-variant.",[18,772,774],{"id":773},"struct-visibility","Struct Visibility",[72,776,778],{"id":777},"why-private-fields-matter","Why private fields matter",[14,780,781,782,784,785,788,789,791,792,795,796,799,800,803,804,807],{},"A ",[34,783,503],{}," struct with ",[29,786,787],{},"private fields"," is the foundation of Rust's encapsulation\u002Fnewtype pattern: external code can ",[84,790,217],{}," the type (call its methods, pass it around) but can't ",[29,793,794],{},"construct"," it with literal syntax or ",[29,797,798],{},"access"," the private fields directly. This lets the module enforce ",[29,801,802],{},"invariants"," — only the module's own constructor\u002Fmethods can build a valid instance, so you can't accidentally create an invalid state from outside. This is how newtypes preserve their guarantees: the constructor is a method that validates, not a public struct literal. Without private fields, any caller could construct a ",[34,805,806],{},"User { email: \"garbage\" }"," bypassing your validation.",[14,809,810,811,813],{},"A struct can be ",[34,812,503],{}," but have private fields — external code can't construct it with literal syntax or access private fields, but can use it via methods. This is how newtypes preserve invariants.",[18,815,817],{"id":816},"module-path-items","Module Path Items",[23,819,820,823,826,829,832,837],{},[26,821,822],{},"Modules",[26,824,825],{},"Functions",[26,827,828],{},"Structs\u002FEnums\u002FTypes",[26,830,831],{},"Constants\u002FStatics",[26,833,834,836],{},[34,835,217],{}," statements",[26,838,839,840,843,844,846],{},"Macros (via ",[34,841,842],{},"macro_rules!"," and ",[34,845,485],{},")",[18,848,850],{"id":849},"submodules-and-privacy","Submodules and Privacy",[72,852,854],{"id":853},"how-the-privacy-model-works","How the privacy model works",[14,856,857,858,861,862,865,866,869,870,872,873,875,876,879],{},"Rust's privacy is ",[29,859,860],{},"per-module-tree",", not hierarchical in the OOP sense. The rule: an item is visible within its own module and all its ",[29,863,864],{},"descendants"," — a child can see its parent's private items, but a parent ",[84,867,868],{},"cannot"," see a child's private items unless the child marks them ",[34,871,503],{},". This is the opposite of \"private = only this class.\" The conceptual basis: a child module is a more-specific piece of the parent's implementation, so it's trusted with the parent's internals; the parent, being more general, isn't automatically trusted with the child's specifics. ",[34,874,503],{}," opens an item up the tree to ancestors and beyond. This is why ",[34,877,878],{},"pub(crate)"," exists for the common case of \"internal to this crate but not exposed to users.\"",[14,881,882,883,885],{},"A child module can access anything in its parent (privacy is per-module-tree, with ",[34,884,503],{}," opening it up). Children can use private items of parents and ancestors.",[18,887,889,891,892],{"id":888},"pub-items-and-dochidden",[34,890,503],{}," Items and ",[34,893,894],{},"#[doc(hidden)]",[14,896,897,899,900,902],{},[34,898,894],{}," hides an item from docs while keeping it ",[34,901,503],{}," (used for internal macros or re-exports you don't want users to call directly).",[18,904,906],{"id":905},"crates-within-a-package","Crates Within a Package",[97,908,910],{"language":909},"toml",[101,911,914],{"className":912,"code":913,"language":909,"meta":105,"style":105},"language-toml shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","# Cargo.toml\n[lib]\nname = \"my_lib\"\npath = \"src\u002Flib.rs\"\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"my_app\"\npath = \"src\u002Fmain.rs\"\n",[34,915,916,921,932,941,949,955,966,974],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,917,918],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,919,920],{"class":115},"# Cargo.toml\n",[109,922,923,926,929],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,924,925],{"class":130},"[",[109,927,928],{"class":126},"lib",[109,930,931],{"class":130},"]\n",[109,933,934,937],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,935,936],{"class":130},"name = ",[109,938,940],{"class":939},"sJ6F3","\"my_lib\"\n",[109,942,943,946],{"class":111,"line":145},[109,944,945],{"class":130},"path = ",[109,947,948],{"class":939},"\"src\u002Flib.rs\"\n",[109,950,951],{"class":111,"line":159},[109,952,954],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":953},true,"\n",[109,956,957,960,963],{"class":111,"line":171},[109,958,959],{"class":130},"[[",[109,961,962],{"class":126},"bin",[109,964,965],{"class":130},"]]\n",[109,967,969,971],{"class":111,"line":968},7,[109,970,936],{"class":130},[109,972,973],{"class":939},"\"my_app\"\n",[109,975,977,979],{"class":111,"line":976},8,[109,978,945],{"class":130},[109,980,981],{"class":939},"\"src\u002Fmain.rs\"\n",[14,983,984,985,988],{},"A package can have many binaries and at most one library. Binaries can use the library via ",[34,986,987],{},"use my_lib::...",".",[18,990,992],{"id":991},"external-crates","External Crates",[97,994,995],{"language":909},[101,996,998],{"className":912,"code":997,"language":909,"meta":105,"style":105},"# Cargo.toml\n[dependencies]\nserde = \"1.0\"\n",[34,999,1000,1004,1013],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,1001,1002],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,1003,920],{"class":115},[109,1005,1006,1008,1011],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,1007,925],{"class":130},[109,1009,1010],{"class":126},"dependencies",[109,1012,931],{"class":130},[109,1014,1015,1018],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,1016,1017],{"class":130},"serde = ",[109,1019,1020],{"class":939},"\"1.0\"\n",[97,1022,1023],{"language":99},[101,1024,1026],{"className":103,"code":1025,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"use serde::Serialize;     \u002F\u002F external crates are in the extern prelude\n",[34,1027,1028],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,1029,1030,1032,1035,1037,1040,1043],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,1031,217],{"class":122},[109,1033,1034],{"class":126}," serde",[109,1036,304],{"class":122},[109,1038,1039],{"class":126},"Serialize",[109,1041,1042],{"class":130},";     ",[109,1044,1045],{"class":115},"\u002F\u002F external crates are in the extern prelude\n",[14,1047,1048,1049,1052,1053,1055],{},"In edition 2018+, you don't need ",[34,1050,1051],{},"extern crate serde;"," — ",[34,1054,217],{}," finds it.",[18,1057,1059],{"id":1058},"workspaces","Workspaces",[72,1061,1063],{"id":1062},"when-to-use-a-workspace","When to use a workspace",[14,1065,1066,1067,1070,1071,1074,1075,1078,1079,1082,1083,1086],{},"A workspace lets multiple crates share a single ",[34,1068,1069],{},"target\u002F"," (disk + compile-time savings), a single ",[34,1072,1073],{},"Cargo.lock"," (unified dependency versions across crates), and unified dependency declarations via ",[34,1076,1077],{},"[workspace.dependencies]",". You reach for a workspace when you have ",[29,1080,1081],{},"multiple related crates"," evolving together: a multi-crate library (core + derive + macros), a monorepo (app + shared internal libs), or a project with separate binary\u002Flibrary\u002Ftooling crates. Keep a single crate when there's only one publishable unit — a workspace adds structure you don't need. Members can depend on each other via ",[34,1084,1085],{},"path = \"..\u002Fcore\""," and stay in sync during local development.",[97,1088,1089],{"language":909},[101,1090,1092],{"className":912,"code":1091,"language":909,"meta":105,"style":105},"# Cargo.toml\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"crates\u002Fapi\", \"crates\u002Fcli\", \"crates\u002Fcore\"]\n",[34,1093,1094,1098,1107],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,1095,1096],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,1097,920],{"class":115},[109,1099,1100,1102,1105],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,1101,925],{"class":130},[109,1103,1104],{"class":126},"workspace",[109,1106,931],{"class":130},[109,1108,1109,1112,1115,1117,1120,1122,1125],{"class":111,"line":134},[109,1110,1111],{"class":130},"members = [",[109,1113,1114],{"class":939},"\"crates\u002Fapi\"",[109,1116,337],{"class":130},[109,1118,1119],{"class":939},"\"crates\u002Fcli\"",[109,1121,337],{"class":130},[109,1123,1124],{"class":939},"\"crates\u002Fcore\"",[109,1126,931],{"class":130},[14,1128,1129,1130,1132,1133,843,1135,1137],{},"Members can depend on each other via ",[34,1131,1085],{},". Shared ",[34,1134,1073],{},[34,1136,1069],{}," directory.",[18,1139,1141],{"id":1140},"macros-across-modules","Macros Across Modules",[72,1143,1145],{"id":1144},"why-macros-need-special-export-treatment","Why macros need special export treatment",[14,1147,1148,1150,1151,1154,1155,1158,1159,1161,1162,1165,1166,1169,1170,1172,1173,184,1176,1179,1180,1183],{},[34,1149,842],{}," macros are ",[29,1152,1153],{},"resolved at a different compilation stage"," than items — they expand ",[84,1156,1157],{},"before"," the module system is fully finalized, so the normal ",[34,1160,503],{}," visibility rules don't apply to them by default. ",[34,1163,1164],{},"#[macro_export]"," opts a macro into crate-wide (and external) visibility by placing it at the ",[29,1167,1168],{},"crate root"," regardless of where it's defined. You reach for ",[34,1171,1164],{}," when you want users of your crate (or other modules within it) to invoke your macro by path (",[34,1174,1175],{},"crate::my_macro!",[34,1177,1178],{},"my_crate::my_macro!","). Use ",[34,1181,1182],{},"pub use my_macro;"," to re-export it under a different module path if you want it visible at a non-root location.",[14,1185,1186,1188,1189,1191],{},[34,1187,842],{}," macros need ",[34,1190,1164],{}," to be used outside their defining module:",[97,1193,1194],{"language":99},[101,1195,1197],{"className":103,"code":1196,"language":99,"meta":105,"style":105},"#[macro_export]\nmacro_rules! my_macro { \u002F* ... *\u002F }\n",[34,1198,1199,1204],{"__ignoreMap":105},[109,1200,1201],{"class":111,"line":112},[109,1202,1203],{"class":130},"#[macro_export]\n",[109,1205,1206,1208,1211,1214,1217],{"class":111,"line":119},[109,1207,842],{"class":126},[109,1209,1210],{"class":126}," my_macro",[109,1212,1213],{"class":130}," { ",[109,1215,1216],{"class":115},"\u002F* ... *\u002F",[109,1218,1219],{"class":130}," }\n",[14,1221,1222,1223,1225],{},"They're exported at the crate root. Use ",[34,1224,1182],{}," to re-export.",[18,1227,1229],{"id":1228},"module-organization-patterns","Module Organization Patterns",[72,1231,1233],{"id":1232},"library-binaries","Library + Binaries",[97,1235,1236],{"language":195},[101,1237,1240],{"className":1238,"code":1239,"language":195,"met